.TH tumd n 0.3 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tumd
.PP
Small dependency\-free Markdown helpers for Tcl.
.PP
\fBtumd\fR covers the Markdown that READMEs, manuals and help files use, for scripts and CI: Markdown\-to\-HTML fragments with GitHub\-style tables, heading extraction, table\-of\-contents generation, and YAML front matter splitting.
.SS Package
.CS
package require tclutils::tumd 0.3
.CE
.SS API
.CS
::tclutils::tumd::toHtml markdown ?option value ...?
::tclutils::tumd::headings markdown
::tclutils::tumd::toc markdown
::tclutils::tumd::frontmatter markdown
::tclutils::tumd::parse markdown ?-lines 0|1?
::tclutils::tumd::inline text ?refs? ?notes?
::tclutils::tumd::paragraph lines ?refs? ?notes?
::tclutils::tumd::unescape html
.CE
.TS
l l.
command	returns
\fBtoHtml\fR	HTML fragment, or a whole page with \fB\-page 1\fR (options below)
\fBheadings\fR	\fB{level text}\fR for each top\-level heading
\fBtoc\fR	Markdown list of links to the headings
\fBfrontmatter\fR	\fB{frontMatterText body}\fR
\fBparse\fR	dict: the blocks of the document, its link definitions and footnotes (below)
\fBinline\fR	HTML of the inline Markdown of one block, with the document's definitions
\fBparagraph\fR	HTML of a paragraph given as its lines (hard breaks as \fB<br>\fR)
\fBunescape\fR	text of such HTML with the entities decoded
.TE
.SS "toHtml options"
.TS
l l.
option	meaning
\fB\-page bool\fR	a complete page: doctype, \fB<head>\fR with title and style, \fB<body>\fR
\fB\-title text\fR	page title; default the front matter \fBtitle:\fR, else the first heading
\fB\-css text\fR	style sheet of the page; default a small one, \fB""\fR for none
\fB\-lang code\fR	\fBlang\fR attribute of the page
\fB\-linkmap {from to ...}\fR	suffix pairs for relative links, e.g. \fB{.md .html}\fR
\fB\-headingoffset n\fR	add \fBn\fR to every heading level (at most 6)
.TE
.CS
set html [::tclutils::tumd::toHtml $md -page 1 -lang de -linkmap {.md .html}]
.CE
.PP
Errors: \fB{TCLUTILS TUMD OPTION name}\fR for an unknown option, \fB{TCLUTILS TUMD VALUE}\fR for a bad value.
.SS "Blocks for viewers and editors"
.PP
\fBparse\fR returns a dict:
.TS
l l.
key	content
\fBblocks\fR	the blocks of the document, the same \fBtoHtml\fR writes (below)
\fBrefs\fR	link reference definitions, for \fBinline\fR and \fBparagraph\fR
\fBnotes\fR	footnotes (key \-> number), for \fBinline\fR and \fBparagraph\fR
.TE
.PP
With \fB\-lines 1\fR also:
.TS
l l.
key	content
\fBlines\fR	\fB{first last}\fR for each top\-level block; lines counted from 1 after the front matter, trailing blank lines not included
\fBdefinitions\fR	\fB{key first last}\fR for each link reference definition (not a block)
\fBoffset\fR	number of lines of the front matter, \fB0\fR without one
.TE
.PP
CRLF and a lone CR count as one line end. Nested blocks (list items, quote and footnote contents) lie within the lines of their top\-level block. A footnote definition is a top\-level block (\fBfootnote\fR).
.TS
l l.
block	content
\fBh level text id\fR	heading; \fBid\fR as in \fBtoHtml\fR
\fBp lines\fR	paragraph lines
\fBcode lang text\fR	fenced or indented code
\fBhr\fR	horizontal rule
\fBquote blocks\fR	block quote
\fBlist ordered start loose items marker\fR	list; item \fB{task blocks}\fR, task \fB""\fR, \fBopen\fR or \fBdone\fR; marker \fB\-\fR, \fB*\fR, \fB+\fR or \fB.\fR, \fB)\fR
\fBtable aligns header rows\fR	table; align \fBleft\fR, \fBcenter\fR, \fBright\fR or \fB""\fR
\fBfootnote key number blocks\fR	footnote definition
\fBcomment text\fR	HTML comment (not shown)
.TE
.PP
Text in blocks is still Markdown. \fBinline\fR (or \fBparagraph\fR for \fBp\fR) turns it into HTML; the definitions are passed explicitly, so several documents can be open at the same time:
.CS
set d [::tclutils::tumd::parse $md]
foreach b [dict get $d blocks] {
    if {[lindex $b 0] eq "p"} {
        puts [::tclutils::tumd::paragraph [lindex $b 1] \
            [dict get $d refs] [dict get $d notes]]
    }
}
.CE
.PP
Without \fBrefs\fR and \fBnotes\fR, reference links and footnote references stay text. \fBtkutils::tkumdview\fR draws a document this way.
.SS "HTML comments"
.PP
Raw HTML is escaped, with one exception: HTML comments are hidden, both as a block (a line starting with \fB<!\-\-\fR, up to the line with \fB\-\->\fR) and inside text (\fBVom <!\-\-f:datum\-\->12.11.2026<!\-\-/f\-\->\fR shows \fBVom 12.11.2026\fR). In code they stay text.
.SS "What is supported"
.PP
Blocks:
.IP \(bu
ATX headings (\fB#\fR to \fB######\fR) and setext headings (a line underlined with \fB===\fR or \fB\-\-\-\fR)
.IP \(bu
paragraphs
.IP \(bu
fenced code blocks using backticks or tildes; indented code (four spaces)
.IP \(bu
blockquotes, also with lazy continuation lines
.IP \(bu
ordered and unordered lists: nested, items continued on indented lines, tight or loose (blank lines between items give \fB<p>\fR inside \fB<li>\fR), start number of an ordered list, task items \fB\- [ ]\fR and \fB\- [x]\fR
.IP \(bu
GitHub\-style tables (see below)
.IP \(bu
horizontal rules
.IP \(bu
link reference definitions (\fB[label]: url "title"\fR), not printed
.IP \(bu
footnotes: \fB[^label]: text\fR, continued by lines indented four spaces
.PP
Inline constructs:
.IP \(bu
code spans, also with a backtick inside (\fB``a`b``\fR)
.IP \(bu
backslash escapes (\fB\e*\fR, \fB\e_\fR, \fB\e|\fR, ...)
.IP \(bu
bold, italic, \fB~~strikethrough~~\fR; emphasis may span a line break
.IP \(bu
links and images, inline with optional title (\fB[t](url "title")\fR) and by reference (\fB[t][label]\fR, \fB[t][]\fR, \fB[label]\fR); a URL may contain parentheses (\fBhttps://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foo_(Bar)\fR)
.IP \(bu
autolinks for URLs and e\-mail addresses (\fB<https://...>\fR, \fB<a@b.de>\fR)
.IP \(bu
bare URLs (\fBhttps://...\fR, \fBwww....\fR) as links; trailing punctuation and an unbalanced \fB)\fR stay outside
.IP \(bu
entities: named (\fB&copy;\fR, \fB&auml;\fR, \fB&euro;\fR, ...) and numeric (\fB&#228;\fR, \fB&#x20AC;\fR); an unknown name and a single \fB&\fR are escaped
.IP \(bu
footnote references \fB[^label]\fR
.IP \(bu
hard line breaks with two trailing spaces or a trailing backslash
.PP
\fBheadings\fR and \fBtoc\fR list the top\-level headings, ATX and setext. CRLF line ends are read like LF.
.SS Footnotes
.CS
Text with a note[^q].

[^q]: The note.
    A second line.
.CE
.PP
Footnotes are numbered in the order of their definitions. A reference becomes \fB<sup id="fnref\-1"><a href="#fn\-1">1</a></sup>\fR; the notes follow at the end as \fB<section class="footnotes">\fR with an \fB<ol>\fR, each \fB<li id="fn\-1">\fR with a link back. A reference without a definition stays text.
.SS Tables
.PP
A table is a header row and a separator row, then body rows until a blank line or another block:
.CS
| Status | Betrag |
|:-------|-------:|
| bezahlt | 1,00 |
.CE
.PP
The separator sets the alignment (\fB:\-\-\fR left, \fB:\-:\fR center, \fB\-\-:\fR right), written as \fBstyle="text\-align:..."\fR on \fB<th>\fR and \fB<td>\fR. Inline markup works in cells, \fB\e|\fR is a literal pipe, short rows are filled with empty cells. Lines with pipes but no separator row stay a paragraph.
.SS "Heading anchors"
.PP
\fBtoHtml\fR gives each heading an \fBid\fR, \fBtoc\fR links to it. The anchor is made as on GitHub: lower case, \fB*\fR and backticks removed, everything but letters, digits, \fB_\fR, \fB\-\fR and blanks removed, blanks become \fB\-\fR. Letters of every script stay (\fBJörg\fR \-> \fBjörg\fR, \fBÜber\fR \-> \fBüber\fR). A repeated anchor gets \fB\-1\fR, \fB\-2\fR, ... (0.2; 0.1 kept only \fBa\-z\fR and \fB0\-9\fR, so \fBJörg\fR and \fBJrg\fR both became \fBjrg\fR).
.SS Limits
.PP
Raw HTML in the input is escaped, not passed through (comments are hidden), so the output is safe to embed. Not supported: definition lists, heading attributes (\fB{#id}\fR), and the finer CommonMark rules for emphasis and list indentation.
.SH FOOTNOTES
.TP
[1]
The note.
A second line.
